"DUTT-7-15-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7015012","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"68ec5fd3f720b892e44bd8faa94c883288a646d42b8681110173ed9c831ba55d","compact":"9033db7fe840e4f0a90c84ba2c6fd6b825343521f2363b753ba2a4a41b53a7c4","nasal":"bd9121e83095174e521707809695a5de2f84c1493ecb2b24303a4a2f751e33e7"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-15-13","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":15,"verse":13,"english":"Seeing his brother in the encounter with his glory obscured through the curse (he had ere this come by), the intelligent (Lord of Yaksas) spoke in words worthy of the line of his grand-father.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-15-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7015013","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b189dde3202efabcae4e2197459d551e6d4b7f18783edebdd14530cf1fe686b1","compact":"9c40dfeccfb5ce1bcafa8219f8b2b04909362847b791cb9c4adb72695c734d58","nasal":"9c40dfeccfb5ce1bcafa8219f8b2b04909362847b791cb9c4adb72695c734d58"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-15-14","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":15,"verse":14,"english":"As, O wicked-minded one, you desistest not, albeit forbidden by me, you shall, afterwards attaining the fruit of this, and repairing to hell, know (the fate that follow there).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.73,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-15-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7015014","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"540f6b19d4dc85e39d6241d99aef9ca64cb3da90c5698e9d64578a48b12811e8","compact":"952b9763bd4575145da25b22849de36f86990a75e27b7ee15f2b0314a5db6a3e","nasal":"952b9763bd4575145da25b22849de36f86990a75e27b7ee15f2b0314a5db6a3e"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-15-15","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":15,"verse":15,"english":"That perverse one, that through ignorance having drunk poison, neglects to adopt proper measures, know the consequence of his act ultimately.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.544,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-15-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7015015","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"115f26c925b2897065a67b16428f45ace8d00e1c41eff7e3db158c02c36f1a60","compact":"7b0227122d2f5628e2bd3354da8a9b6b0cb1978b5c03c9582d49d7a0b090bc0a","nasal":"7b0227122d2f5628e2bd3354da8a9b6b0cb1978b5c03c9582d49d7a0b090bc0a"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-15-16","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":15,"verse":16,"english":"The gods have set their face against you on account of a certain misdeed of your; and having for this, been reduced to this condition, you do not understand things.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.639,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-15-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7015016","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4ba8c2240b801ca161492dffe4f28b7a727f8642394837568ff2026e821889b1","compact":"ba986aadb16b5c8915c3749e550a4bcdd7f7b9a292d6217ab7b976638db83763","nasal":"7491a1bbc3509596c1d36ddcf1483d137ec1870255506e533afb5886feff2263"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-15-17","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":15,"verse":17,"english":"He that dishonour his father and mother* and spiritual preceptor, reap the fruit of his act on coming under the sway of the sovereign of the dead. *Unless he serve his parents, his heart does not incline to piety.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.344,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-15-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7015017","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a0827dfa4d94ed15bf4f1a6fc281e5f20f5ee1c1dcb5d07d8b87aa86cfe94219","compact":"6ace6c5a989996c2e7186d07ddfd3182b3d7dc2f56bce60ba8ca4e013367e6a7","nasal":"6ace6c5a989996c2e7186d07ddfd3182b3d7dc2f56bce60ba8ca4e013367e6a7"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-15-18","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":15,"verse":18,"english":"Having regard that this body is uncertain, that foolish person, that does not acquire asceticism, dying go the way that he deserve.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.672,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-15-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7015018","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f201707cdc9160f0a3445c92e39d77f99cd88d5df4afb34d308bdd5dd478d09d","compact":"3232f0f0498377bc4ec0d8cb06c99762f6182cb4711ea6f8873f1384ed0d6922","nasal":"3232f0f0498377bc4ec0d8cb06c99762f6182cb4711ea6f8873f1384ed0d6922"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-15-19","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":15,"verse":19,"english":"The mind of a perverse man does not willingly incline towards good; and as he acts, he gets the fruits (he reaps as he sows).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.75,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-15-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7015019","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3c0a8a2b27c4e4e9a2f37e27cb28577ebc43a3d4798de44ceed1c3f5e907a3ad","compact":"84501fd2247e8c1d62de954ea79fba196dd05c56a6b26789e5d80b8c95cc10ac","nasal":"e022b9d7ca57fd8c79319d399c6ae2e4c37a8899aa8c3f378bacc5471b0deb23"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-15-20","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":15,"verse":20,"english":"In this world people, making their own good fortune and beauty, strength, sons, wealth and valour, gain these by virtue of their pious acts.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.16,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-15-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7015020","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ab3b02020f1018b6ee0066ea05e62b7dd5e540d4ef014fad4fcf1ebf8c9380fe","compact":"af6791150758bf30b59c9fbd172f115e0ef99e47f7ed29a4fdaf8fe8e2443402","nasal":"82c6496056c0a8c88e39e66911611ecd57cf12f8e0c2fed9058fc48c8988912e"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-15-21","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":15,"verse":21,"english":"Being given to such iniquitous acts, you will go to hell; and your designs being such, I will not hold parley with you.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.677,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-15-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7015021","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d768de564eaee38f9df32ca8280423b2d70727682ab6bef037c1f8ec7eb0a442","compact":"8233f30fedd43ac13f572f46177cd1a70351bed3da44ea84d45864d2c403e649","nasal":"8233f30fedd43ac13f572f46177cd1a70351bed3da44ea84d45864d2c403e649"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-15-22","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":15,"verse":22,"english":"Honest people should act carefully in connection with the wicked.' Thus reprimanded by him, his (Rāvana's) councillors, headed by Marica, on being struck, took to their heels.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.851,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-15-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7015022","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3a2913965272de7e43edf330ded312df2c6742ee4cc7d84d85d420e1bd20e864","compact":"0590b3437eed04aed38f19fa81934627a8c5e57613afb75fa199314308a60f4c","nasal":"0590b3437eed04aed38f19fa81934627a8c5e57613afb75fa199314308a60f4c"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-15-23","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":15,"verse":23,"english":"Then Daśagrīva on being Struck in the head with the mace by the lord of Yakşas, did not move from his place.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.841,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-15-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7015023","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6ff1d16dfe16f0c65d4a14fc1cee3b0f9c921cbfe7e92cb2a81ef12a03818fe5","compact":"402a9a7e6a45f2efead36d5cc488907c23837c9d10c370bd77520cfac7c0d546","nasal":"f61608409e2bf7f890bda26c585471e8e07ca233244f7763b952251e5ac6ab7b"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-15-24","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":15,"verse":24,"english":"And then, O Rama, the Yaksa and Raksasa, smiting each other in mighty encounter, did not get bewildered of experience fatigue.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.322,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-15-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7015024","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4ba193f75b11bfaa6a447fbe9c46b4742727ee3ebc2ec70e3ab23f97340915b8","compact":"ed9a91b92360bbc4b3e59721b7452bdbfb4a0e5fe652c098b48ed5f2a10c0e0f","nasal":"0ef47804166a3d2be2cc7eae65909b132c25a703a2342908e8db2c32a5d70b1b"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-15-25","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":15,"verse":25,"english":"And then the bestower of riches discharged a fiery weapon at him; and thereat the lord of Rāks asa resisted it with a Varuņa weapon.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.172,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-15-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7015025","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0db1a659159451d91fb11fa24316af83caac81a69aad1f50776c47587aacbc5f","compact":"2771f1b73a19f695feba19a090c061b798a010d2c16275bf591f88e947e03ea4","nasal":"2771f1b73a19f695feba19a090c061b798a010d2c16275bf591f88e947e03ea4"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-15-26","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":15,"verse":26,"english":"Thus he wore full many forms and he was not visible in his native shape. And then, O Rāma, seizing a mighty weapon the Ten-necked one, whirling the same, brought that redoubtable mace down on the head of the bestower of riches.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.333,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-15-32"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7015026","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"de27fb09bb0aceb2a20f0c062f330caef660de4916b30b7218c818f08f1b23fa","compact":"b2b9686883d6f41a4d13c56d56f3df790759d58b03a334601ddfffe165517fa1","nasal":"b2b9686883d6f41a4d13c56d56f3df790759d58b03a334601ddfffe165517fa1"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-15-27","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":15,"verse":27,"english":"Thus smitten by him, the lord of wealth, baffled, toppled down to the earth covered with blood like an aśoka whose roots have been hewn away.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-15-33"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7015027","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cdb12beedb2571eed08c87ec09866aecb35b9bdc8684b02fe4b19f4bd4df4a01","compact":"fc9773790716fe79ddac07f9bc3711755b18ec1e0b17815f30f8237170762304","nasal":"fc9773790716fe79ddac07f9bc3711755b18ec1e0b17815f30f8237170762304"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-15-28","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":15,"verse":28,"english":"Thereat Padma and other Nidhi deities, surrounding the granter the granter of wealth, raised him up and brought him to the Nandana wood.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.382,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-15-34"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7015028","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b72ca511671ba46abd3be602b156451668b2c5bae7a9f5362efcf8e164672140","compact":"332ce962954630f4d70452a0af886bfea03eb20c337efbdd22c1c8e883b88f10","nasal":"5b753615c08771e9929d746af560f8da94de1ecb8100562b27f30ee4663f0d21"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-15-29","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":15,"verse":29,"english":"Conquering the bestower of wealth, the lord of Raksasas, with a delighted heart, possessed himself of his Puspaka, the car, as a sign of victory; furnished with golden pillars, gateways set with lapises, covered with networks of pearls, having three yielding the fruits of all seasons, endowed with the celerity of thought, ranging everywhere at will, wearing forms at pleasure, capable of coursing in the sky, with golden and jewelled stairs, and daises of polished gold, the vehicle of the gods undeteriorating, bringing delight to the mind and sight; wonderous exceedingly: painted with images designed to fill the mind with reverence, constructed by Brahmä, containing all objects of desire, charming and nonpariel not cold and not yet hot, granting gratification in every season, and graceful to the view. And ascending that (car) coursing at will, won by his prowess, that utterly wicked one, out of swelling insolence, deemed himself master of the three worlds. And having vanquished the deity Vaiśravaņa, he descended from Kailasa.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.491,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-15-35"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7015029","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1009bc85414a22df5e60c14c360ac2564b53d277a57129d990c73904a4e3e4e9","compact":"4b94e7a8730cbc0829712f0178b9534260e177b09ec63b1d2b0fc5aa1bf3a2de","nasal":"4b94e7a8730cbc0829712f0178b9534260e177b09ec63b1d2b0fc5aa1bf3a2de"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-15-30","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":15,"verse":30,"english":"Conquering the bestower of wealth, the lord of Raksasas, with a delighted heart, possessed himself of his Puspaka, the car, as a sign of victory; furnished with golden pillars, gateways set with lapises, covered with networks of pearls, having three yielding the fruits of all seasons, endowed with